% You are an expert TypeScript React engineer. Build `pdd/frontend/components/DeploymentsPanel.tsx`, an opt-in PDD Connect panel for services running on a local Kubernetes cluster.

% Dependencies
<deployments_dependencies>
  <include>pdd/frontend/api.ts</include>
</deployments_dependencies>

% Concept
Dev Units are implementation units, not pods. A service is a deployable unit that a developer has explicitly mapped one or more Dev Units onto, declared in `.pdd/deployments.yaml`. This panel shows that mapping and the resulting workload health. It is not a general Kubernetes dashboard.

% Requirements
1. Export default `DeploymentsPanel` as a React functional component.
2. On mount, call `api.getDeployments()`. Render nothing at all while loading, when `plugin_installed` is false, or when `configured` is false, so projects that never need containers are unaffected.
3. For each service, show its name, deploy state badge, the Dev Units it carries, ready/desired replicas, restart count, port, per-pod health and node, and any recent failure events.
4. Provide Deploy/Redeploy, Stop and Logs actions per service. Deploy and Stop return an operation record; append it to a recent-actions list showing action, service, state and any failure message.
5. While any operation is `running`, poll for fresh status every few seconds and disable the action buttons; clear the interval on unmount.
6. Show logs on demand via `api.getDeploymentLogs(service)` in a closable, scrollable preformatted block.
7. Surface an unreachable cluster as an inline message while still listing the statically declared services and their Dev Units.
8. Handle request failures by showing an inline error, never by throwing.
9. Use responsive Tailwind dark/glass styling consistent with the Connect app shell.

% Security constraints
- Display only data returned by the deployments API; do not read browser storage or project files directly.
- Render logs and event text as plain text; never inject them as HTML.

% Deliverable
- Output only `pdd/frontend/components/DeploymentsPanel.tsx`.
